aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Frequency switching: the line sits on the other side of the band centre and
    the baseline is fitted outside +-180 km/s, so broad structure beside the
    line no longer bends it.
  * Settings: receiver gain for each stage, a switch to ignore pulsed
    interference (off by default) and a switch to smooth the calibrated plot
    (on by default). The measured peak is never taken from the smoothed line.
  * Search tabs say when a node observes the hydrogen line only.
  * The log and block table say hits, not candidates, before tiering.
  * Status says when the receiver is missing instead of capturing.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0530

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A node observing the hydrogen line alone opens on the Hydrogen line tab.
  * Settings: switch for frequency switching, on by default. Calibrate now
    says when its reference is not used.
  * Settings and Quick setup: closing the dialog waits for its receiver scan,
    so cancelling quickly cannot crash the app.
  * The first scan message no longer asks for a calibration when none is needed.
  * A scan with no measurement is no longer marked calibrated.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0530

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hydrogen line only mode: frequency switching, no calibration needed. The
    tab shows which calibration is in use, with an info button.
  * Hydrogen line in dB above baseline, shown beside the raw plot.
  * Median filter n and m in Settings.
  * Hydrogen line only mode keeps retrying a failed capture.
  * Windows: the capture tool ends with the app, so a crash cannot leave the
    radio locked until a reboot.
  * Settings: switch to let other computers on the network see this node.
  * Node API keeps retrying when its address is not up yet at boot.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 17:45:00 +0530

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Linux: the window's class name now equals the launcher entry, which is
    what GNOME matches on X11, so the dock and switcher show the app's icon.
    0.2.8 changed the wrong half of the pair.

